    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110038\">Kevin Buzzard</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/579631-Lean-Releases/topic/v4.2E31.2E0/near/607547657\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Fintype#doc\">docs#Fintype</a> is in mathlib so this is probably better asked in <a class=\"stream\" data-stream-id=\"287929\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4\">#mathlib4</a> -- the Lean bump will also have entailed a mathlib bump which is presumably your actual problem.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I see, there is strict coupling between the Mathlib version and the Lean version and I first got this today with the 4.31 update so didn't consider it necessary to report as a standalone Mathlib4 issue. This being said I would like to move it as early as possible but don't have permission to move a message to a different channel. Perhaps you have these permissions or could at least confirm what I reported is a genuine issue without a straightforward answer so I can just open a new topic?</p>",
