    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"221653\">Paul Reichert</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/v4.2E31.2E0/near/607594833\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Does this minimized example also fail on 4.30-rc1? At least it produces the same synthesization failure on v4.28.1, which is the only old version I had readily available via <a href=\"https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=JYWwDg9gTgLgBAWQIYwBYBtgCMBQOAmApgGZwAycAFAMJwBccgqIQCU9cAKgJ5iH0C8cAN5wAHmzLAAzvEoAxYADs4AZlYB6NeSkwAdOkIKA5mlFwBtAL55F0pAoDGvBvIUxuvShWqs6fHHDgXNx4dCGIAUQBHAFdgADcqCWkdADVCexhoKhcVVm8qKNi4nSgSdDgAfWY8SUIYCogwGGAIJRgoJEcdBDqkHUlOV1QASQVbB1526N5FHAVW%2BwhwaJgkLH04G1WJtgBlaLBdusS4fN9%2FOEAL8mJopUkzAD4qSR1Ml1qYZh1iCHR8KgA7XBAClEcABrEApUSbfCAS%2FIcEA&amp;project=mathlib-v4.28.0\">Lean4Web</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Very interesting point! This was a contrived example and the code that I have did in fact work with all previous versions and only turned into an error once I updated to 4.31 yesterday. So I dug deeper and now I suspect that version 4.31 is in fact unhiding some error that might have been hiding before. I tried other mwe-s with even more similar types and unfortunately I could not extract any improvements that would produce the exact same behavior.</p>\n<p>This being said, it is still not clear to me why the above error would happen still even though now there is a high likelihood that this is indeed not related to the version at all and 4.31 only improves in that regard.</p>",
